    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jonathan Aranda** (64.59) and **Dylan Beavers** (63.81) headline our offensive output. **Jonathan Aranda** is a premier start against Gray, as his projection is bolstered by a massive 12% platoon advantage and a solid #2 spot in the order, allowing him to capitalize on early-game opportunities. Meanwhile, **Dylan Beavers** benefits significantly from the matchup against Brown, where a 7% platoon lift and an elevated spot in the order push him into our elite tier. **Cal Raleigh** remains our highest-scoring asset at 72.64; while Ray presents a fair test, the combination of a favorable 4.95 xERA and a generous 19% SP skill boost makes **Cal Raleigh** our most reliable producer for power metrics today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Tyler Freeman** (46.09) out of the starting nine. While his park factor is enticing, the model ultimately faded him due to a high-end matchup against a tough Greene, coupled with a bottom-third order placement that stifles his total point expectation. Elsewhere, **Geraldo Perdomo** (60.89) narrowly maintains his spot over our deeper depth pieces, primarily due to his high-leverage #2 order placement and an efficient matchup against Pallante. We are exercising caution with **Bryce Harper** (57.80) and **Daulton Varsho** (55.48), as both face challenging arms in McLean and Burke; however, their base projections remain too high to justify benching. Investors should monitor weather closely, but as of now, the primary risk remains the high-caliber arms of Greene and Gilbert potentially neutralizing the upside of **Tyler Freeman** and **Jung Hoo Lee** should we need to pivot late.",
